# Docker build context filter for the pnpm-workspace image builds.
#
# cranker/Dockerfile and evidence-daemon/Dockerfile build from the repo ROOT
# (they need pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, and packages/sdk). This file
# keeps that context small and stops stale artifacts from poisoning `pnpm install`.

# Dependencies & build outputs (materialized inside the image)
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.cache
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tgz

# Rust / Anchor / Solana (programs are built out-of-band, never in these images)
target
programs
.anchor
test-ledger
.surfpool
Cargo.toml
Cargo.lock
rust-toolchain.toml
Anchor.toml
Makefile

# Unrelated workspace members: exclude their SOURCE to keep the context lean,
# but KEEP their package.json — `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` validates the
# whole workspace graph, so a missing manifest fails it. (Note: we exclude
# `dir/*` not `dir` — excluding the dir node itself makes re-inclusion impossible.)
apps/app/*
!apps/app/package.json
apps/landing/*
!apps/landing/package.json
tests/*
!tests/package.json
# apps/docs is MkDocs (no package.json); pnpm skips it in the apps/* glob.
apps/docs

# VCS & editor
.git
.github
.idea
.vscode

# Docs, secrets, local cruft
*.md
!packages/sdk/README.md
.agents
.claude
.beans.yml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
context
meta
